		<name>How About a Nice Game of Chess</name>
		<sortname>2096 =-  How About a Nice Game of Chess</sortname>
		<desc>Chess 7.5, a.k.a. "How about a nice game of chess!" (1984) is an early C64 program written by Larry Atkin, most famous for co-writing the Chess 3.x and 4.x series of programs that ruled the world of computer chess in most of the 70s.</desc>
		<rating>0.73</rating>
