	<game>
		<path>./5-verylow/Frogger.crt</path>
		<name>Frogger (Parker Brothers)</name>
		<sortname>3510 =-  Frogger (Parker Brothers)</sortname>
		<desc>Your task in this arcade game is to guide a frog across a treacherous road and river, and to safety at the top of the screen. Both these sections are fraught with a variety of hazards, each of which will kill the frog and cost you a life if contact is made. The road is full of cars and trucks, at variable speeds. The river water itself is fatal, as are the snakes which hover within on later levels. Frogger must use the arrangement of logs, turtles (which are only there for a short time) and alligators (but stay away from their faces), and then jump into one of the open home-cells, ideally one containing a fly for extra points. Once all holes have been filled, you move onto the next, harder, level.
Of the nearly a dozen Frogger versions put out for the Commodore 64, the two primary versions of this game were the Parker Brothers version that had better box graphics and marketing and the Sierra Online version, which is generally considered to have superior game graphics and play.</desc>
		<rating>0.80</rating>
